  (global_label "SPK_MINUS" (shape passive) (at 261.62 142.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid "397ad68d-9576-51cb-8a6e-bd1c3490b61a")
    (property "Intersheetrefs" "" (at 261.62 142.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide)))
  (text "Power: the switch common is the 3.3 V rail (XIAO 3V3 pin and the sounder driver). Position 1 = badge 3.3 V feeds the rail. Position 2 (OFF) ties D1 to the rail through R4; position 3 (USB-BAT) leaves the badge disconnected." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 160.02 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9acc96ca-fbc0-59bf-bc81-3787826d553a"))
  (text "On USB-BAT the XIAO powers the rail itself, from USB-C or the LiPo on J2 (which it charges). Do not plug in USB with the switch on SAO while on a badge: two 3.3 V regulators would share one rail." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 163.83 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "8a4f2337-b859-5046-851f-5572d38255cb"))
  (text "Sounder driver (replaces the maker's amplifier): D10 -> R1 1.3k -> Q1 base. Q1 switches the sounder's minus side to ground. R5 || R6 (2 x 330 = 165 ohm) from 3.3 V limit the current to 19 mA whatever the sounder is." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 167.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9b228173-7d5b-57ce-b9e6-e2c37c6388c5"))
  (text "D1 (flyback) catches the coil's kick if the sounder is magnetic; R7 1.3k discharges it if it is a piezo. Both are harmless for the other type." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 171.45 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "12d12d4a-e3f2-5b64-9ba5-39767f06f88e"))
  (text "R2, R3: 330 ohm on the SAO GPIO pins per docs/standard.md. R4: 330 ohm in the OFF sense line. R1, R2, R4 each let one other track pass between their pads: the board is routed on the back copper only." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 175.26 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "50304deb-3803-5936-98e1-64bd57164472"))
  (text "The maker's ATtiny85, its reset pull-up R1 4k7, C1 100 nF, the ISP pads and his amplifier (C2 22 uF, R2 2k2, BC847) are replaced by the XIAO and the driver above. Mode button = the XIAO's BOOT button." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 179.07 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "33752c24-a508-50cb-83c8-48f0e44a8303"))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
)
